# November 24, 2026: Ticonderoga, Essex County, New York: the old paper-mill village on the La Chute River and the fort.
# Aimed at the Adirondacks by the owner's channel as a test of which research tools can reach their sites; start.py found
# no Atlas place in Ticonderoga village (12 listed places, 2 districts) and only a thin landmark pin for the fort.
# Sources were opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py) for the Register buildings; HMdb marker
# pages for the La Chute Riverwalk panels (125097, 125100, 125183, 125185, 158199, 158927, 314052); the Town of Ticonderoga's
# parks, Frazier Bridge and Heritage Museum pages; Fort Ticonderoga's hours and Carillon Battlefield pages; Essex County's
# tourism listings for Hancock House and the La Chute River Walk. Those web pages were read with the web fetch tool,
# because the shell could not reach them. NPGallery could not be reached, so no Register form was read.
